           `pyVmomi.vim.host.Capability.vmDirectPathGen2UnsupportedReason` and/or in
           `pyVmomi.vim.host.Capability.vmDirectPathGen2UnsupportedReasonExtended`.
       vmDirectPathGen2UnsupportedReason: If `pyVmomi.vim.host.Capability.vmDirectPathGen2Supported` is false, this array will be
           populated with reasons for the lack of support (chosen from
           `pyVmomi.vim.host.Capability.VmDirectPathGen2UnsupportedReason`).
           
           If there is a reason for
           the lack of support that cannot be described by the available constants,
           `pyVmomi.vim.host.Capability.vmDirectPathGen2UnsupportedReasonExtended` will be populated
           with an additional explanation provided by the platform.
           
           Note that this list of reasons is not guaranteed to be exhaustive.
           
           If the reason \"hostNptIncompatibleProduct\" is provided, then that will
           be the only provided reason, as the host software is incapable of
           providing additional information.
       vmDirectPathGen2UnsupportedReasonExtended: If `pyVmomi.vim.host.Capability.vmDirectPathGen2Supported` is false, this property may
           contain an explanation provided by the platform, beyond the reasons (if
           any) enumerated in `pyVmomi.vim.host.Capability.vmDirectPathGen2UnsupportedReason`.
       supportedVmfsMajorVersion: List of VMFS major versions supported by the host.
       vStorageCapable: Indicates whether the host supports vStorage Hardware
           acceleration.
       snapshotRelayoutSupported: Indicates whether this host supports unrestricted relocation of virtual
           machines with snapshots.
           
           Only needs to be true on the destination host for
           the unrestricted relocation to work. The full snapshot relocation does not
           restrict the layout of snapshot files or disks of the virtual machine, nor
           its power state. If the virtual machine is powered on, a storage vmotion
           will be performed to relocate its snapshots and disks.
       firewallIpRulesSupported: Indicates whether this host supports ip address based restrictions in
           the firewall configuration.
       servicePackageInfoSupported: Indicates whether this host supports package information in service
           configuration.
       maxHostRunningVms: The maximum number of virtual machines that can be run on the host.
           
           An unset value indicates that the value could not be obtained. In contrast
           to `pyVmomi.vim.host.Capability.maxRunningVMs`, this value is the minimum of (i) the maximum
           number supported by the hardware and (ii) the maximum number permitted by
           the host license.
       maxHostSupportedVcpus: The maximum number of virtual CPUs that can be run on the host.
           
           An unset
           value indicates that the value could not be obtained. In contrast to
           `pyVmomi.vim.host.Capability.maxSupportedVcpus`, this value is the minimum of (i) the maximum
           number supported by the hardware and (ii) the maximum number permitted by
           the host license.
       vmfsDatastoreMountCapable: Indicates whether the host is capable of mounting/unmounting
           VMFS datastores.
       eightPlusHostVmfsSharedAccessSupported: Indicates whether the host is capable of accessing a VMFS disk
           when there are eight or more hosts accessing the disk already.
       nestedHVSupported: Indicates whether the host supports nested hardware-assisted virtualization.
       vPMCSupported: Indicates whether the host supports virtual CPU performance counters.
       interVMCommunicationThroughVMCISupported: Indicates whether the host supports VMCI for communication
           between virtual machines.
       scheduledHardwareUpgradeSupported: Indicates whether the host supports scheduled hardware upgrades.
       featureCapabilitiesSupported: Indicated whether the host supports feature capabilities
           for EVC mode.
       latencySensitivitySupported: Indicates whether the host supports latency sensitivity for the
           virtual machines.
       storagePolicySupported: Indicates that host supports Object-based Storage System and
           Storage-Profile based disk provisioning.
       accel3dSupported: Indicates if 3D hardware acceleration for virtual machines is supported.
       reliableMemoryAware: Indicates that this host uses a reliable memory aware allocation policy.
       multipleNetworkStackInstanceSupported: Indicates whether the host supports Multiple Instance TCP/IP stack
       messageBusProxySupported: Indicates whether the message bus proxy is supported
       vsanSupported: Indicates whether the host supports VSAN functionality.
       vFlashSupported: Indicates whether the host supports vFlash.
       hostAccessManagerSupported: Whether this host supports HostAccessManager for controlling direct
           access to the host and for better lockdown mode management.
       provisioningNicSelectionSupported: Indicates whether a dedicated nic can be selected for vSphere Provisioning
           NFC traffic.
       nfs41Supported: Whether this host supports NFS41 file systems.
       nfs41Krb5iSupported: Whether this host support NFS41 Kerberos 5* security type.
       turnDiskLocatorLedSupported: Indicates whether turning on/off local disk LED is supported
           on the host.
       virtualVolumeDatastoreSupported: Indicates whether this host supports VirtualVolume based Datastore.
       markAsSsdSupported: Indicates whether mark disk as SSD or Non-SSD is supported
           on the host.
       markAsLocalSupported: Indicates whether mark disk as local or remote is supported
           on the host.
       smartCardAuthenticationSupported: Indicates whether this host supports local two-factor user
           authentication using smart cards.
       pMemSupported: Indicates whether this host supports persistent memory.
           
           If value is not specified, it should be considered as not supported.
       pMemSnapshotSupported: Indicates whether this host supports snapshots for VMs with virtual
           devices backed by persistent memory.
           
           If value is not specified, it should be considered as not supported.
       cryptoSupported: Flag indicating whether Cryptographer feature is supported.
       oneKVolumeAPIsSupported: Indicates whether this host supports granular datastore cache update.
           
           If value is not specified, it should be considered as not supported.
       gatewayOnNicSupported: Flag indicating whether default gateway can be configured on a
           vmkernel nic.
       upitSupported: Indicate whether this host supports UPIT
       cpuHwMmuSupported: Indicates whether this host supports hardware-based MMU virtualization.
       encryptedVMotionSupported: Indicates whether this host supports encrypted vMotion.
       encryptionChangeOnAddRemoveSupported: Indicates whether this host supports changing the encryption state
           of a virtual disk when the disk is being added or removed from a
           virtual machine configuration.
       encryptionHotOperationSupported: Indicates whether this host supports changing the encryption state
           of a virtual machine, or virtual disk, while the virtual machine
           is powered on.
       encryptionWithSnapshotsSupported: Indicates whether this host supports changing the encryption state
           state of a virtual machine, or virtual disk, while the virtual
           machine has snapshots present.
       encryptionFaultToleranceSupported: Indicates whether this host supports enabling Fault Tolerance on
           encrypted virtual machines.
       encryptionMemorySaveSupported: Indicates whether this host supports suspending, or creating
           with-memory snapshots, encrypted virtual machines.
       encryptionRDMSupported: Indicates whether this host supports encrypting RDM backed virtual
           disks.
       encryptionVFlashSupported: Indicates whether this host supports encrypting virtual disks with
           vFlash cache enabled.
       encryptionCBRCSupported: Indicates whether this host supports encrypting virtual disks with
           Content Based Read Cache (digest disks) enabled.
       encryptionHBRSupported: Indicates whether this host supports encrypting virtual disks with
           Host Based Replication enabled.
       ftEfiSupported: Indicates whether this host supports Fault Tolerance VMs that have
           specified UEFI firmware.
       unmapMethodSupported: Indicates which kind of VMFS unmap method is supported.
           
           See
           `pyVmomi.vim.host.Capability.UnmapMethodSupported`
       maxMemMBPerFtVm: Indicates maximum memory allowed for Fault Tolerance virtual machine.
       virtualMmuUsageIgnored: Indicates that `pyVmomi.vim.vm.FlagInfo.virtualMmuUsage` is
           ignored by the host, always operating as if \"on\" was selected.
       virtualExecUsageIgnored: Indicates that `pyVmomi.vim.vm.FlagInfo.virtualExecUsage` is
           ignored by the host, always operating as if \"hvOn\" was selected.
       vmCreateDateSupported: Indicates that createDate feature is supported by the host.
       vmfs3EOLSupported: Indicates whether this host supports VMFS-3 EOL.
           
           If value is not specified, it should be considered as not supported.
       ftVmcpSupported: Indicates whether this host supports VMCP for Fault Tolerance VMs.
       quickBootSupported: Indicates whether this host supports the LoadESX feature
           which allows faster reboots.
       encryptedFtSupported: Indicates whether this host supports encrypted Fault Tolerance.
           
           Since: vSphere API Release 7.0.2.0
       assignableHardwareSupported: Indicates whether this host supports Assignable Hardware.
       suspendToMemorySupported: Indicates whether this host supports suspending virtual machines to memory.
           
           Since: vSphere API Release 7.0.2.0
       useFeatureReqsForOldHWv: Indicates whether this host uses vmFeatures for compatibility checking
           of old (8 or lower) virtual hardware version VMs.
       markPerenniallyReservedSupported: Indicates whether this host supports marking specified LUN as
           perennially reserved.
       hppPspSupported: Indicates whether this host supports HPP path selection policy
           settings.
       deviceRebindWithoutRebootSupported: Indicates whether device rebind without reboot is supported.
           
           This is
           the capability which enables PCI passthrough and SR-IOV configuration
           without reboot.
       storagePolicyChangeSupported: Indicates whether this host supports storage policy change.
       precisionTimeProtocolSupported: Indicates whether this host supports date time synchronization over
           Precision Time Protocol (PTP).
       remoteDeviceVMotionSupported: Indicates whether vMotion of a VM with remote devices attached is
           supported.
           
           This applies to CD-ROM and floppy devices backed by a
           remote client.
       maxSupportedVmMemory: The maximum amount of virtual memory supported per virtual machine.
           
           If this capability is not set, the size is limited by hardware version
           of the virtual machine only.
       ahDeviceHintsSupported: Indicates if the host supports Assignable Hardware device hints.
           
           Since: vSphere API Release 7.0.2.0
       nvmeOverTcpSupported: Indicates if access to NVMe over TCP devices is supported.
           
           Since: vSphere API Release 7.0.3.0
       nvmeStorageFabricServicesSupported: Indicates whether NVMe Storage Fabrics Services (StFS) are supported.
           
           Since: vSphere API Release 7.0.3.0
       assignHwPciConfigSupported: Indicates if setting hardwareLabel using PciPassThrough is supported.
           
           Since: vSphere API Release 7.0.2.0
       timeConfigSupported: Indicates whether advanced timekeeping apis are supported
           
           Since: vSphere API Release 7.0.3.0
       nvmeBatchOperationsSupported: Indicates whether batch NVMe controller connection/disconnection is supported.
           
           See `pyVmomi.vim.host.StorageSystem.connectNvmeControllerEx` and
           `pyVmomi.vim.host.StorageSystem.disconnectNvmeControllerEx`.
           
           Since: vSphere API Release 7.0.3.0
       pMemFailoverSupported: Indicates whether this host supports failover for VMs with virtual
           devices backed by persistent memory.
           
           If value is not specified, it should be considered as not supported.
           
           Since: vSphere API Release 7.0.2.0
       hostConfigEncryptionSupported: Indicates whether this host supports host configuration encryption.
           
           Since: vSphere API Release 7.0.2.0
       maxSupportedSimultaneousThreads: Max supported number of SMT (Simultaneous multithreading) threads.
           
           If value is not specified, it should be considered as not supported.
           
           Since: vSphere API Release 8.0.0.1
       ptpConfigSupported: Indicates whether this host supports PTP (Precision Time Protocol)
           service configuration.
           
           See `pyVmomi.vim.host.PtpConfig`. If value is
           not specified, it should be considered as not supported.
           
           Since: vSphere API Release 7.0.3.0
       maxSupportedPtpPorts: Number of PTP (Precision Time Protocol) ports supported by this
           host (See `pyVmomi.vim.host.PtpConfig`).
           
           If this capability is not
           set, number of PTP ports in the host is 0.
           
           Since: vSphere API Release 7.0.3.0
       sgxRegistrationSupported: Indicates whether this host supports SGX registration.
           
           Since: vSphere API Release 8.0.0.1
       pMemIndependentSnapshotSupported: Indicates whether this host supports snapshots of VMs configured
           with independent vNVDIMMs.
           
           If value is not specified, it should be considered as not supported.
           This support does not depend on `pyVmomi.vim.host.Capability.pMemSnapshotSupported`.
           
           Since: vSphere API Release 7.0.3.0
       iommuSLDirtyCapable: Indicates whether this host's IOMMUs are capable of tracking pages
           written by device DMAs using dirty bits in the second-level page
           tables.
           
           If this value is not specified, it should be considered as
           not capable.
           
           Since: vSphere API Release 8.0.0.1
       vmknicBindingSupported: Indicates whether vmknic binding is supported over this host.
           
           Since: vSphere API Release 8.0.1.0
       ultralowFixedUnmapSupported: Indicates whether ultralow fixed unmap bandwidth is supported on this host.
           
           Since: vSphere API Release 8.0.0.1
       nvmeVvolSupported: Indicates whether mounting of NVMe vvol is supported on this host.
           
           Since: vSphere API Release 8.0.0.0
       fptHotplugSupported: Indicates whether FPT Hotplug is supported on this host.
           
           Since: vSphere API Release 8.0.1.0
       mconnectSupported: Indicates whether MCONNECT is supported on this host.
           
           Since: vSphere API Release 8.0.1.0
       vsanNicMgmtSupported: Indicates whether vSAN nic types can be managed by VirtualNicManager.
           
           Since: vSphere API Release 8.0.2.0
       vvolNQNSupported: Indicates whether vVol NQN is supported on this host.
           
           Since: vSphere API Release 8.0.2.0
       stretchedSCSupported: Indicates whether \"stretched\" vVol Storage Container is supported on this host.
           
           Since: vSphere API Release 8.0.3.0
       vmknicBindingOnNFSv41: Indicates whether vmknic binding is supported on NFSv41 over this host.
           
           Since: vSphere API Release 8.0.3.0
       vpStatusCheckSupported: Indicates whether VasaProvider Status can be monitored on the host.
           
           Since: vSphere API Release 8.0.3.0
       e2e4knSupported: Indicates whether E2E 4KN capability is supported on the host.
           
           Since: vSphere API Release 9.0.0.0
       vsanDedicatedVmkNicSupported: Indicates whether vSAN external vmknic configuration is supported on the host.
           
           Since: vSphere API Release 9.0.0.0
       nConnectSupported: Indicates whether NFS41 NCONNECT is supported on this host.
           
           Since: vSphere API Release 8.0.3.0
       userKeySupported: Indicates whether user-provided private key installation is supported on this host.
           
           Since: vSphere API Release 8.0.3.0
       ndcmSupported: Indicates whether non-disruptive certificate management is supported on this host.
           
           Since: vSphere API Release 8.0.3.0
       uefiSecureBoot: Flag indicating that the firmware reports the use of UEFI Secure
           Boot during system boot.
           
           TPM attestation may be used to definitively determine the boot
           time UEFI Secure Boot state and its complete configuration. An
           out-of-band management channel may also be considered.
           
           Since: vSphere API Release 8.0.3.0
       vpxdVmxGenerationSupported: Indicates whether this host can populate and consume
           `pyVmomi.vim.vm.ConfigInfo.vmxRuntimeConfig` property.
           
           Since: vSphere API Release 9.0.0.0
       nfs41Krb5pSupported: Indicates whether this host supports NFS41
           encryption using KRB5P protocol.
           
           Since: vSphere API Release 9.0.0.0
       cimSupported: Indicates whether this host supports CIM
           
           Since: vSphere API Release 9.0.0.0
       npivSupported: Indicate whether this host supports NPIV
           
           Since: vSphere API Release 9.0.0.0
       entitlementSupported: Indicates whether this host supports license entitlements
           
           Since: vSphere API Release 9.0.0.0
       monitorUnrestricted: Flag indicating that the host is using unrestricted monitor mode.
           
           If False or unset, the monitor mode is not fully supported with certain
           VM types when the Memory Tiering is enabled.
           
           Since: vSphere API Release 9.1.0.0
       vnetworkingNicSelectionSupported: Flag indicates whether a dedicated nic can be selected for vnetworking traffic.
           
           Since: vSphere API Release 9.1.0.0
       directPathInfoSupported: Indicates whether the host provides information about DirectPath devices
           on the host.
           
           If false or unset, then the host does not provide DirectPath
           device information.
           
           Since: vSphere API Release 9.1.0.0
       fcdLinkedCloneSupported: Indicates whether \"FCD Linked Clone feature\" supported on this host.
           
           Since: vSphere API Release 9.1.0.0
       ehvQuickBootSupported: Indicates whether the quick boot is supported on EHV (encrypted hardware
           virtualization) capable hosts.
           
           Since: vSphere API Release 9.1.0.0
       nestedHvTieringEnabled: Flag indicating that the host can run nested hypervisor with Memory
           Tiering enabled.
           
           If false or unset, the host does not support nested hypervisor
           with Memory Tiering enabled.
           
           Since: vSphere API Release 9.1.0.0
   """
   class ReplayUnsupportedReason(pyVmomi.VmomiSupport.Enum):
      """
