           You can use the `pyVmomi.vim.Datastore.Summary` property if the `pyVmomi.vim.host.MountInfo`
           property is not set. The VirtualCenter Server will always make
           sure the `pyVmomi.vim.Datastore.Summary` property is set correctly.
       inaccessibleReason: This optional property for inaccessible reason is reported only if
           a datastore becomes inaccessible as reported by
           `pyVmomi.vim.host.MountInfo.accessible` and
           `pyVmomi.vim.Datastore.Summary`.`pyVmomi.vim.Datastore.Summary.accessible`.
           
           The values for inaccessible reason are defined in the enum
           `pyVmomi.vim.host.MountInfo.InaccessibleReason`
           This helps to determine host specific reason for datastore inaccessibility.
           If the datastore becomes accessible following an inaccessible condition,
           the property `pyVmomi.vim.host.MountInfo.inaccessibleReason` will be unset.
       vmknicName: The name of the vmknic used during mount for NFSv3 datastore.
           
           Populated by the vmk control layer if the NAS
           volume is mounted successfully with a vmknic binding.
           In case of NFS v4.1, if vmknic binding is enabled successfully,
           then output will be in format {hostip1:vmknic1, hostip2:vmknic2}.
           If vmknic binding is not enabled, then vmknicName
           will have 'None' string.
           
           Since: vSphere API Release 8.0.1.0
       vmknicActive: Indicates whether vmknic is active or inactive.
           
           This field will be populated by vmk control layer during
           NAS volume mount, and will be set to true if the
           vmknic binding is active.
           
           Since: vSphere API Release 8.0.1.0
       mountFailedReason: The optional property which gives the reason for mount operation
           failure of NFS datastore.
           
           This field is applicable for only those
           mounts for which retry mount operation is configured.
           The values for the mount failed reason are defined in the enum
           `pyVmomi.vim.host.MountInfo.MountFailedReason`.
           If mount operation on NFS volume succeeds in the retry, then
           the property `pyVmomi.vim.host.MountInfo.mountFailedReason` will be unset.
           
           Since: vSphere API Release 8.0.0.1
       numTcpConnections: Maintained for each Host, it indicates the total number of TCP
           connections for the NAS datastore
           
           Since: vSphere API Release 8.0.1.0
   """
   class AccessMode(pyVmomi.VmomiSupport.Enum):
      """
      Defines the access mode of the datastore.
      
      Attributes:
          readWrite: The host system has read/write access to the file system.
          readOnly: The host system has read-only access to the file system.
      """
      readWrite: _typing.ClassVar['MountInfo.AccessMode'] = 'readWrite'
      readOnly: _typing.ClassVar['MountInfo.AccessMode'] = 'readOnly'

   class InaccessibleReason(pyVmomi.VmomiSupport.Enum):
      """
      A datastore can become inaccessible due to a number of reasons as
      defined in this enum `pyVmomi.vim.host.MountInfo.InaccessibleReason`.
      
      The reason for a datastore being inaccessible is reported in
      `pyVmomi.vim.host.MountInfo.inaccessibleReason`.
      APD (\"All Paths Down\") is a condition where a SAN or NFS storage has
      become inaccessible for unknown reasons. It only indicates loss of
      connectivity and does not indicate storage device failure or
      LUN removal (Permanent Device Loss or PDL)
      A difference between APD and PDL is that APD may recover
      in which case all use cases will start to work as before. In case of PDL
      the failed datastore/device is unlikely to recover and hence the device
      path information and data cache will be emptied. If the PDL condition
      recovers, the failed datastores have to be added back to the host. Once
      in PDL a datastore cannot be added back until there are no longer any
      open files on the datastore.
      PDL is not linked to the APD and can happen at any time with or without APD
      preceding. If APD and PDL occur at the same time, APD will be reported first.
      Once (and if) the APD condition clears, PermanentDataLoss will be reported if
      PDL condition still exists.
      
      Attributes:
          AllPathsDown_Start: AllPathsDown_Start value is reported when all paths down state is detected
          AllPathsDown_Timeout: After a wait for a system default time (which is user modifiable)
              to ascertain the state is indeed an APD, AllPathsDown_Timeout property
              is reported.
              
              The host advanced option used to set timeout period
              is \"/Misc/APDTimeout\"
              After the datastore property is set to AllPathsDown_Timeout, all data i/o
              to the datastore will be fast-failed (failed immediately).
          PermanentDeviceLoss: A PDL condition is reported as PermanentDeviceLoss.
      """
      AllPathsDown_Start: _typing.ClassVar['MountInfo.InaccessibleReason'] = 'AllPathsDown_Start'
      AllPathsDown_Timeout: _typing.ClassVar['MountInfo.InaccessibleReason'] = 'AllPathsDown_Timeout'
      PermanentDeviceLoss: _typing.ClassVar['MountInfo.InaccessibleReason'] = 'PermanentDeviceLoss'

   class MountFailedReason(pyVmomi.VmomiSupport.Enum):
      """
      NFS mount request can be failed due to a number of reasons as
      defined in this enum `pyVmomi.vim.host.MountInfo.MountFailedReason`.
      
      The reason for the mount failure is reported in
      `pyVmomi.vim.host.MountInfo.mountFailedReason`. This is applicable only for those
      datastores to which mount retry is configured.
      
      Attributes:
          CONNECT_FAILURE: Failed to get port or connect.
              
              Or MOUNT/FSINFO RPC failed.
          MOUNT_NOT_SUPPORTED: Server doesn't support MOUNT_PROGRAM/MOUNT_PROGRAM_VERSION.
          NFS_NOT_SUPPORTED: Server doesn't support NFS_PROGRAM/NFS_PROGRAM_VERSION.
          MOUNT_DENIED: No permission to mount the remote volume or it doesn't exist.
          MOUNT_NOT_DIR: Remote path not a directory.
          VOLUME_LIMIT_EXCEEDED: Maximum NFS volumes have been mounted.
          CONN_LIMIT_EXCEEDED: Maximum connections for NFS has been reached.
          MOUNT_EXISTS: Volume already mounted or a different mount exists with same label.
          OTHERS: Any other reason which is not present in above list.
      
      Since: vSphere API Release 8.0.0.1
      """
      CONNECT_FAILURE: _typing.ClassVar['MountInfo.MountFailedReason'] = 'CONNECT_FAILURE'
      MOUNT_NOT_SUPPORTED: _typing.ClassVar['MountInfo.MountFailedReason'] = 'MOUNT_NOT_SUPPORTED'
      NFS_NOT_SUPPORTED: _typing.ClassVar['MountInfo.MountFailedReason'] = 'NFS_NOT_SUPPORTED'
      MOUNT_DENIED: _typing.ClassVar['MountInfo.MountFailedReason'] = 'MOUNT_DENIED'
      MOUNT_NOT_DIR: _typing.ClassVar['MountInfo.MountFailedReason'] = 'MOUNT_NOT_DIR'
      VOLUME_LIMIT_EXCEEDED: _typing.ClassVar['MountInfo.MountFailedReason'] = 'VOLUME_LIMIT_EXCEEDED'
      CONN_LIMIT_EXCEEDED: _typing.ClassVar['MountInfo.MountFailedReason'] = 'CONN_LIMIT_EXCEEDED'
      MOUNT_EXISTS: _typing.ClassVar['MountInfo.MountFailedReason'] = 'MOUNT_EXISTS'
      OTHERS: _typing.ClassVar['MountInfo.MountFailedReason'] = 'OTHERS'

   path: _typing.Optional[str] = None
   accessMode: str
   mounted: _typing.Optional[bool] = None
   accessible: _typing.Optional[bool] = None
   inaccessibleReason: _typing.Optional[str] = None
   vmknicName: _typing.Optional[str] = None
   vmknicActive: _typing.Optional[bool] = None
   mountFailedReason: _typing.Optional[str] = None
