          netStackInstanceKey: The NetStackInstance that the virtual NIC uses, the value of this property
              is default to be `defaultTcpipStack`
          opaqueNetwork: Opaque network (`pyVmomi.vim.host.OpaqueNetworkInfo`) to which the
              virtual NIC is connected.
              
              When reconfiguring a virtual NIC, this property indicates the specification
              of opaque network to which the virtual NIC should connect. You can specify
              this property only if you do not specify `pyVmomi.vim.host.VirtualNic.Specification.distributedVirtualPort`
              and `pyVmomi.vim.host.VirtualNic.Specification.portgroup`.
          externalId: An ID assigned to the vmkernel adapter by external management plane.
              
              The value and format of this property is determined by external management
              plane, and vSphere doesn't do any validation. It's also up to external
              management plane to set, unset or maintain this property.
              
              This property is applicable only when `pyVmomi.vim.host.VirtualNic.Specification.opaqueNetwork` property is set,
              otherwise it's value is ignored.
          pinnedPnic: The physical nic to which the vmkernel adapter is pinned.
              
              Setting this value
              ensures that the virtual NIC will access external network only via the
              the specified physical NIC.
              
              This property is applicable only when `pyVmomi.vim.host.VirtualNic.Specification.opaqueNetwork` property is set.
              If the vmkernel adapter is connected to a portgroup or dvPort, then such
